1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,840
It smells good.

2
00:00:13,660 --> 00:00:15,180
You should smell the lily, too.

3
00:00:16,080 --> 00:00:16,960
Sniff, sniff.

4
00:00:17,800 --> 00:00:19,460
All set. Are you girls ready?

5
00:00:20,120 --> 00:00:21,800
Try to smile pretty for me.

6
00:00:25,080 --> 00:00:26,720
Okay, say cheese.

7
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,620
From the beginning, we hated you.

8
00:00:34,060 --> 00:00:37,420
But also, we loved you from the beginning as well.

9
00:00:38,020 --> 00:00:41,120
All we wanted was to become true friends with you.

10
00:00:41,580 --> 00:00:43,380
So we had to cross the wall.

11
00:00:43,900 --> 00:00:46,240
I had to have you all to myself.

12
00:00:48,240 --> 00:00:49,000
Kirikuma!

13
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:54,600
Kirikuma Urochi!

14
00:02:26,021 --> 00:02:33,701
Delicious smell, slurp.

15
00:02:37,801 --> 00:02:41,921
Good morning, Kureha. Growl, growl.

16
00:02:44,501 --> 00:02:50,181
Kinko, good morning. Growl, growl. Lick?

17
00:02:50,181 --> 00:02:55,981
Kureha, you're close to me.

18
00:02:58,621 --> 00:03:00,781
Wait a minute. What are you doing?

19
00:03:02,921 --> 00:03:05,641
Seriously, why are you in my house again?

20
00:03:06,321 --> 00:03:07,881
I moved in, growl.

21
00:03:08,941 --> 00:03:12,541
Growl, growl! All done! We're finished moving in!

22
00:03:17,481 --> 00:03:19,261
We're your roomies now.

23
00:03:19,261 --> 00:03:20,901
Bottoms up!

24
00:03:26,061 --> 00:03:28,041
New roomie noodles!

25
00:03:28,841 --> 00:03:30,701
Come on, Kureha.

26
00:03:30,941 --> 00:03:32,521
Bottoms up!

27
00:03:32,921 --> 00:03:34,381
New roomie noodles!

28
00:03:35,901 --> 00:03:38,081
Get out!

29
00:03:38,761 --> 00:03:40,981
Get out of my house!

30
00:03:43,981 --> 00:03:45,621
You have to leave.

31
00:03:45,621 --> 00:03:48,961
And by the way, it's not acceptable to just move into someone's house without asking.

32
00:03:48,961 --> 00:03:50,021
Growl, growl!

33
00:03:50,021 --> 00:03:52,601
But Kureha, you ate your new roomie noodles!

34
00:03:53,801 --> 00:03:56,001
So, I don't even get what that means.

35
00:03:56,001 --> 00:03:59,141
Look, it's that one girl.

36
00:03:59,141 --> 00:04:02,141
What? Oh, her. She's totally bad luck to her friends.

37
00:04:02,141 --> 00:04:09,321
It's worse than bad luck. Students are disappearing. And the missing girls all happen to be from her class.

38
00:04:09,321 --> 00:04:13,321
There, you heard them. Getting close to me is bad luck.

39
00:04:15,001 --> 00:04:18,561
It's true. You're gonna get caught up in the invisible storm.

40
00:04:18,561 --> 00:04:21,201
Do you really believe that?

41
00:04:21,201 --> 00:04:31,841
Yes. If you two make friends with me, you'll just wind up excluded. Because that's the law of this herd. Understand now? Leave me alone for your own sake.

42
00:04:31,841 --> 00:04:43,681
Growl, growl, growl! You're the one who doesn't understand, silly. Lulu told you, Ginkgo, and Lulu came here to make friends with you!

43
00:04:43,681 --> 00:04:51,881
We'll protect Kureha from the invisible storm. And we promise we won't back down on love. Growl, growl.

44
00:04:51,881 --> 00:05:00,781
I'm not lying. She was a bear masquerading as a human.

45
00:05:01,181 --> 00:05:02,221
That's impossible.

46
00:05:02,721 --> 00:05:09,861
I saw it. Mitsuko turned into a bear right in front of me. She ate Sumika. She killed my friend.

47
00:05:10,741 --> 00:05:14,941
Mitsuko told me as much herself. And then... And then I...

48
00:05:14,941 --> 00:05:23,541
I took my gun. And I aimed it right at her?

49
00:05:24,841 --> 00:05:28,161
Kureha. That's enough of this story.

50
00:05:28,361 --> 00:05:29,141
But it's true!

51
00:05:29,641 --> 00:05:34,041
You poor darling. The shock was just too much, so you've clearly hallucinated.

52
00:05:34,221 --> 00:05:35,501
No, it's real! I swear!

53
00:05:35,901 --> 00:05:43,021
I won't force you to do anything right away. However, you will eventually need to accept the reality of the situation and let it go.

54
00:05:43,021 --> 00:05:50,621
I just remembered. Next Sunday is your birthday. It is, isn't it?

55
00:05:52,081 --> 00:05:52,561
Yes.

56
00:05:52,921 --> 00:06:00,241
Rhea's little girl about to be 17. I can't believe it. Time certainly flies. So tell me, what would you like to do this year?

57
00:06:00,681 --> 00:06:03,161
Go out for dinner? Or did you want a particular present?

58
00:06:04,461 --> 00:06:06,321
No. Not this year.

59
00:06:06,321 --> 00:06:16,041
Now that I think about it, you know your mother's pendant? She loved it so much. It was a present for her when she turned 17.

60
00:06:16,481 --> 00:06:18,441
I'm actually the one who gave it to her.

61
00:06:19,181 --> 00:06:20,501
Really? It was from you?

62
00:06:20,961 --> 00:06:28,041
Yes. It was a symbol of a promise between friends. We pledged to each other that we would never forget love.

63
00:06:28,421 --> 00:06:30,301
You pledged to never forget love?

64
00:06:30,301 --> 00:06:35,861
We sure did. As long as you don't forget love, you'll never ever be truly alone.

65
00:06:36,261 --> 00:06:41,921
And if you don't give up on love, even if you lose something, you'll never be invisible.

66
00:06:42,721 --> 00:06:49,841
Of course, it's important to know that love can cause us pain as well. For example, when we remember time that's been lost.

67
00:06:50,521 --> 00:06:52,801
Remember time that's been lost?

68
00:06:52,801 --> 00:07:02,801
Sumika.

69
00:07:02,801 --> 00:07:03,441
Sumika.

70
00:07:04,161 --> 00:07:09,381
Whenever we feel that pain, we should try to focus on something else and not be too hard on ourselves.

71
00:07:09,841 --> 00:07:14,641
Koreha, I think what you probably need right now more than anything is a new friend.

72
00:07:15,261 --> 00:07:17,041
A new friend? Seriously?

73
00:07:17,581 --> 00:07:21,121
Yes. Try allowing yourself to get close to someone else.

74
00:07:21,221 --> 00:07:22,081
I can't do it.

75
00:07:22,081 --> 00:07:22,401
What?

76
00:07:23,061 --> 00:07:29,921
I don't want to get close to someone else. Sumika is my only friend. I'll never give up on love, no matter what.

77
00:07:29,921 --> 00:07:35,941
Grow, growl, munch munch

78
00:07:35,941 --> 00:07:38,061
Grow, growl, munch munch

79
00:07:38,061 --> 00:07:39,721
Grow, growl, munch munch

80
00:07:39,721 --> 00:07:42,681
Grow, growl, curry pie is eating one of those rolls again

81
00:07:42,681 --> 00:07:45,121
But Lulu doesn't think they smell all that delicious

82
00:07:45,121 --> 00:07:47,481
Krayha eats what tastes like love to her

83
00:07:47,481 --> 00:07:49,001
What tastes like love?

84
00:07:49,141 --> 00:07:51,281
Yes, it's something which can't be destroyed

85
00:07:51,281 --> 00:07:53,121
By any storm or bear or human

86
00:07:53,121 --> 00:07:55,581
Say what? Are you sure that's for real?

87
00:07:55,941 --> 00:07:57,501
It's real, I'm sure

88
00:07:59,921 --> 00:08:29,901
I don't know.

89
00:08:29,921 --> 00:08:43,121
It's okay. I'm your friend. You don't have to be alone anymore. I'm here, and I love you. Lady Kumaria.

90
00:08:45,621 --> 00:08:52,541
I remember getting love from someone. That's why I came. Why I crossed the wall.

91
00:08:53,681 --> 00:08:58,561
Kureha, I want to have you. I want you all to myself.

92
00:08:59,921 --> 00:09:07,921
Hey, Kureha. Got a sec, maybe?

93
00:09:10,701 --> 00:09:16,681
I want you to know. We talked it over this morning. Everyone agreed we've been really cruel.

94
00:09:17,381 --> 00:09:20,701
We know we're in the wrong, and we're beyond sorry for what we've done.

95
00:09:20,701 --> 00:09:28,121
So, we want to make it up to you. Not just you. To Sumika, too.

96
00:09:28,121 --> 00:09:37,321
Give me a break. You all excluded, Sumika. None of you have the right to be forgiven.

97
00:09:37,821 --> 00:09:41,681
Why the change of heart now? If this is some sort of game, you girls better finish it.

98
00:09:41,901 --> 00:09:45,961
Because I won't lose to people like you. You're not going to make me invisible.

99
00:09:45,961 --> 00:09:54,341
Please, please forgive us. We've all been so... We've been so awful. We really are sorry.

100
00:09:58,881 --> 00:10:02,541
What was that, Growl? Only we get to make friends with Kureha.

101
00:10:02,761 --> 00:10:05,021
That girl is in our way. Big time.

102
00:10:05,581 --> 00:10:08,581
Only one solution. Growl, Growl.

103
00:10:08,581 --> 00:10:23,281
Hey, listen to this. Article 1. The way to a girl's heart is through her stomach.

104
00:10:24,281 --> 00:10:30,001
Challenge accepted. Ginkgo and Lulu are going to make curry pie something she loves as much as those crazy rolls.

105
00:10:30,001 --> 00:10:33,641
And then... Lulu is so clever.

106
00:10:34,781 --> 00:10:38,401
Delicious smell. Growl, Growl.

107
00:10:38,581 --> 00:10:42,641
No! You can't transform here. It doesn't matter how hungry you may be.

108
00:10:42,861 --> 00:10:47,621
We have to follow court rules on this side. We're only allowed to eat the flesh of invisible girls, Ginkgo.

109
00:10:48,441 --> 00:10:48,961
Growl.

110
00:10:50,541 --> 00:10:53,041
So do you know what kinds of food Kureha likes?

111
00:10:53,341 --> 00:10:54,741
Shiokara and spaghetti.

112
00:10:55,761 --> 00:10:57,841
That sounds like what an old man would eat.

113
00:10:58,321 --> 00:10:59,901
She's liked them since she was little.

114
00:11:00,381 --> 00:11:04,181
Hmm. All right. Guess we know what tonight's dinner will be.

115
00:11:08,581 --> 00:11:12,501
Growl, Growl! Welcome home, lady!

116
00:11:13,181 --> 00:11:14,641
Um, what are you doing?

117
00:11:15,301 --> 00:11:17,061
Making dinner. Growl, Growl.

118
00:11:17,121 --> 00:11:20,701
Uh-huh. Ginkgo and Lulu have decided to make your love flavor.

119
00:11:21,641 --> 00:11:23,721
Make what? My love flavor?

120
00:11:23,721 --> 00:11:28,261
Yep! We're cooking your two favorite foods!

121
00:11:28,601 --> 00:11:29,921
What? No way!

122
00:11:31,701 --> 00:11:34,321
Yes! We call it Shiokara spaghetti!

123
00:11:34,861 --> 00:11:36,521
Delicious smell, Growl, Growl.

124
00:11:36,901 --> 00:11:38,581
Oh, wow! Incredible!

125
00:11:39,261 --> 00:11:41,421
A flavor-pairing made in heaven!

126
00:11:42,681 --> 00:11:44,841
Try one, Ginkgo! Cherry tomato!

127
00:11:44,841 --> 00:11:51,581
Here comes Ginkgo! Try some creamy honey flan!

128
00:11:52,921 --> 00:11:58,141
Eat this, Ginkgo! Creamy, lightly salted salmon!

129
00:12:01,641 --> 00:12:03,341
Now it's your turn, Growl!

130
00:12:05,281 --> 00:12:07,121
No thanks. I won't eat that.

131
00:12:07,441 --> 00:12:07,781
What?

132
00:12:07,781 --> 00:12:17,801
But why? We thought you were a fan of Shiokara and spaghetti, just like old men are!

133
00:12:18,561 --> 00:12:20,401
Wait. How'd you know that?

134
00:12:20,481 --> 00:12:21,781
We... did?

135
00:12:22,141 --> 00:12:24,841
I'm certain I only ever told Sumika about that.

136
00:12:25,261 --> 00:12:27,221
Two transfer students shouldn't know anything.

137
00:12:27,881 --> 00:12:29,381
Hmm. Good point!

138
00:12:29,761 --> 00:12:31,021
We don't know anything.

139
00:12:31,081 --> 00:12:33,621
I'm serious. I want you to stay away from me!

140
00:12:33,621 --> 00:12:36,241
Growl, but we want to be a sense, Curry pie!

141
00:12:36,241 --> 00:12:38,021
Why is that so hard to understand?

142
00:12:38,201 --> 00:12:38,921
Stop it!

143
00:12:41,261 --> 00:12:43,821
Enough about being my friend. I'm sick of it.

144
00:12:44,021 --> 00:12:46,481
Why is everyone trying to make me give up on my love?

145
00:12:46,761 --> 00:12:49,061
How many times do I have to repeat myself?

146
00:12:49,341 --> 00:12:51,161
I don't want new friends.

147
00:12:51,661 --> 00:12:53,281
Sumika is my only love.

148
00:12:53,501 --> 00:12:55,241
I don't want anyone else.

149
00:12:55,961 --> 00:12:57,101
What's with you two?

150
00:12:57,441 --> 00:12:59,981
Why are you so damn desperate to get close to me?

151
00:13:01,921 --> 00:13:02,881
Growl, Growl!

152
00:13:02,881 --> 00:13:04,761
That was super scary for Lulu.

153
00:13:04,761 --> 00:13:09,321
Lulu thought for sure you were about to tell Curry pie the truth about everything.

154
00:13:10,621 --> 00:13:15,081
But you know, Ginko, if you tell her, we can't be human girls anymore.

155
00:13:15,941 --> 00:13:17,581
Those are the court's rules.

156
00:13:19,041 --> 00:13:19,601
Sheesh!

157
00:13:19,821 --> 00:13:21,881
Lulu hopes Curry pie remembers you soon.

158
00:13:22,001 --> 00:13:23,341
This is getting exhausting.

159
00:13:24,701 --> 00:13:26,261
Ginko, I'm here.

160
00:13:26,761 --> 00:13:27,941
Your love!

161
00:13:27,941 --> 00:13:32,181
Listen about earlier.

162
00:13:33,181 --> 00:13:33,801
I'm sorry.

163
00:13:33,981 --> 00:13:34,861
I was happy.

164
00:13:35,261 --> 00:13:37,501
I just had a hard time admitting it.

165
00:13:39,141 --> 00:13:40,001
Growl, Growl.

166
00:13:40,141 --> 00:13:40,701
It's okay.

167
00:13:41,061 --> 00:13:41,841
I understand.

168
00:13:42,561 --> 00:13:46,301
I was thinking, if we took some time to wash each other all over,

169
00:13:46,601 --> 00:13:49,081
it might give us the chance to really get to know one another.

170
00:13:49,081 --> 00:13:51,761
Gorgeous snow.

171
00:13:55,761 --> 00:13:57,561
What about that, Ginko?

172
00:13:57,861 --> 00:13:59,061
Does it feel good?

173
00:13:59,181 --> 00:14:00,741
Growl, yeah, it feels good.

174
00:14:01,001 --> 00:14:02,221
And here, Ginko?

175
00:14:02,741 --> 00:14:03,421
This spot?

176
00:14:03,641 --> 00:14:04,681
Does it feel good?

177
00:14:05,101 --> 00:14:06,441
Oh yeah, it does.

178
00:14:07,081 --> 00:14:07,921
Really good.

179
00:14:08,361 --> 00:14:09,601
And what about here?

180
00:14:09,601 --> 00:14:11,681
How does this spot feel?

181
00:14:12,081 --> 00:14:13,101
Really good.

182
00:14:13,501 --> 00:14:15,741
Oh yeah, really good.

183
00:14:15,741 --> 00:14:17,761
It's, it's amazing.

184
00:14:21,701 --> 00:14:23,861
Here you go, Queen Esa-wistle!

185
00:14:36,481 --> 00:14:37,621
Here, Kureha.

186
00:14:37,901 --> 00:14:38,621
For you.

187
00:14:40,961 --> 00:14:42,721
I know it's a little early.

188
00:14:43,081 --> 00:14:43,781
What's that?

189
00:14:43,901 --> 00:14:45,681
My birthday isn't for a while, you know.

190
00:14:46,141 --> 00:14:47,301
Yeah, of course I do.

191
00:14:47,601 --> 00:14:48,661
I can't explain it.

192
00:14:48,861 --> 00:14:50,421
I just had to give you this today.

193
00:14:50,721 --> 00:14:52,661
Okay, you are so silly.

194
00:14:52,841 --> 00:14:53,361
Um, wait.

195
00:14:53,761 --> 00:14:54,741
Don't open it yet.

196
00:14:55,321 --> 00:14:55,621
What?

197
00:14:56,361 --> 00:14:58,701
On your birthday, I want you to come to this spot.

198
00:14:58,921 --> 00:15:00,261
Then you can read what it says.

199
00:15:00,921 --> 00:15:01,761
Why then?

200
00:15:02,101 --> 00:15:04,561
So that it's perfect, since it's my present to you.

201
00:15:04,981 --> 00:15:06,021
You got me a gift?

202
00:15:06,021 --> 00:15:07,361
How could I not?

203
00:15:08,081 --> 00:15:09,221
Wait though to open it?

204
00:15:09,821 --> 00:15:10,101
Please?

205
00:15:11,181 --> 00:15:12,721
Yeah, sure thing.

206
00:15:13,061 --> 00:15:13,801
Look at you.

207
00:15:13,801 --> 00:15:16,481
Oh, such a beautiful smile.

208
00:15:16,921 --> 00:15:18,821
I want you to always smile like that.

209
00:15:19,021 --> 00:15:19,721
Like a flower.

210
00:15:20,161 --> 00:15:21,181
That's my love.

211
00:15:21,701 --> 00:15:22,261
It's funny.

212
00:15:22,701 --> 00:15:26,901
Even if I had to watch you from a distance, I would be happy just to see that smile.

213
00:15:27,141 --> 00:15:28,341
What are you talking about?

214
00:15:28,561 --> 00:15:30,001
There's no distance between us.

215
00:15:30,041 --> 00:15:31,241
I'm always right by your side.

216
00:15:31,701 --> 00:15:32,441
That's true.

217
00:15:32,441 --> 00:15:36,181
So, you kept your promise and didn't back down on love.

218
00:15:36,501 --> 00:15:38,761
I'll never, ever forget that either.

219
00:15:40,401 --> 00:15:40,921
Sumika?

220
00:15:43,501 --> 00:15:45,701
They'll bloom soon, won't they?

221
00:15:46,461 --> 00:15:47,001
Yeah.

222
00:15:47,001 --> 00:15:49,881
Oh, Sumika.

223
00:15:50,381 --> 00:15:51,581
You're my only friend.

224
00:15:51,981 --> 00:15:53,501
And the only friend I want.

225
00:15:59,501 --> 00:16:00,661
The flower bed.

226
00:16:00,661 --> 00:16:03,881
We asked the school to help you grow flowers again.

227
00:16:04,621 --> 00:16:06,361
I'm sorry about what happened yesterday.

228
00:16:07,721 --> 00:16:09,861
We all are really sorry, Koriha.

229
00:16:11,401 --> 00:16:14,661
The invisible storm wrecked this place, but we want to fix it now.

230
00:16:14,881 --> 00:16:16,061
We'll do whatever it takes.

231
00:16:16,341 --> 00:16:18,101
Our thought was to refill it with flowers.

232
00:16:18,621 --> 00:16:22,061
We were hoping we could work together to make Sumika's last wish come true.

233
00:16:22,881 --> 00:16:23,821
Last wish?

234
00:16:23,941 --> 00:16:25,281
What do you know about it?

235
00:16:25,281 --> 00:16:29,281
Well, we know it has to do with your birthday, which is next week, right?

236
00:16:29,641 --> 00:16:31,041
Yeah, that's right.

237
00:16:31,641 --> 00:16:37,701
You see, I heard that before, uh, before what happened to Sumika happened, that she said, um...

238
00:16:37,701 --> 00:16:38,181
What?

239
00:16:38,921 --> 00:16:40,481
She said she wanted a party.

240
00:16:40,901 --> 00:16:41,661
One for you.

241
00:16:41,921 --> 00:16:44,181
And she wanted it in a garden full of flowers.

242
00:16:45,381 --> 00:16:48,101
So that it's perfect, since it's my present to you.

243
00:16:50,381 --> 00:16:50,861
Sumika.

244
00:16:50,861 --> 00:16:55,381
Well, we're asking you to allow us to celebrate your birthday this year.

245
00:16:55,921 --> 00:16:57,121
Because that...

246
00:16:57,121 --> 00:16:59,061
That's what Sumika wanted.

247
00:17:02,001 --> 00:17:04,701
Please, for Sumika's sake.

248
00:17:04,701 --> 00:17:21,641
Oh, what's with that?

249
00:17:21,941 --> 00:17:24,961
Bingo and Lulu are her friends, not those stinking girls.

250
00:17:25,601 --> 00:17:26,521
You agree, yeah?

251
00:17:26,521 --> 00:17:26,601
Yeah.

252
00:17:26,601 --> 00:17:35,861
We don't have much time before Kureha's birthday.

253
00:17:36,221 --> 00:17:37,981
Let's start today, okay, girls?

254
00:17:38,061 --> 00:17:38,561
Okay!

255
00:17:38,561 --> 00:17:38,881
Okay!

256
00:17:38,881 --> 00:18:06,161
Ladies, thank you for working so hard these past few days.

257
00:18:06,161 --> 00:18:11,961
Because of everyone here, Kureha Tsubaki has started to believe that we are interested in being her friends.

258
00:18:12,281 --> 00:18:14,481
We only need to endure her a little longer.

259
00:18:14,901 --> 00:18:18,141
At this moment, we will confirm our feelings and make a final decision.

260
00:18:18,801 --> 00:18:20,741
Who is the evil we must exclude?

261
00:18:22,021 --> 00:18:23,381
Let's search evil!

262
00:18:34,001 --> 00:18:34,561
Select.

263
00:18:36,161 --> 00:18:39,221
We have chosen Kureha Tsubaki as the evil to exclude.

264
00:18:41,081 --> 00:18:41,841
